WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.478
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.513
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:16.865
Unit twenty-six: Wish and If only. Today you will express regrets and wishes about the present and the past.

4
00:00:17.165 --> 00:00:19.852
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.882
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:25.509
Wish.

7
00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:28.981
Wish means to want something that is not true.

8
00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:31.095
I wish I had a car.

9
00:00:31.683 --> 00:00:34.254
Your turn. Say: Wish.

10
00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.008
Wish.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.856
If only.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.815
If only means a stronger wish.

13
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:45.033
If only I could fly!

14
00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:47.886
Your turn. Say: If only.

15
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:51.874
If only.

16
00:00:52.617 --> 00:00:53.757
Present regret.

17
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.284
Present regret means sadness about the present.

18
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.395
I wish I were taller.

19
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:03.332
Your turn. Say: Present regret.

20
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:07.446
Present regret.

21
00:01:08.183 --> 00:01:09.370
Past regret.

22
00:01:10.383 --> 00:01:13.347
Past regret means sadness about a past action.

23
00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.450
I wish I had called.

24
00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.377
Your turn. Say: Past regret.

25
00:01:21.233 --> 00:01:22.443
Past regret.

26
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:23.813
Would.

27
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.327
Would means wish + would for annoying habits.

28
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:29.289
I wish he would stop.

29
00:01:29.883 --> 00:01:31.990
Your turn. Say: Would.

30
00:01:34.833 --> 00:01:35.521
Would.

31
00:01:36.283 --> 00:01:36.948
Were.

32
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.437
Were means used for all persons after wish.

33
00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:42.492
I wish I were rich.

34
00:01:43.083 --> 00:01:45.155
Your turn. Say: Were.

35
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.769
Were.

36
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:50.495
Had done.

37
00:01:51.483 --> 00:01:54.156
Had done means past perfect for a past wish.

38
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.215
I wish I had done it.

39
00:01:56.817 --> 00:01:59.039
Your turn. Say: Had done.

40
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:02.924
Had done.

41
00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:04.870
Impossible.

42
00:02:05.883 --> 00:02:08.022
Impossible means cannot happen.

43
00:02:08.617 --> 00:02:09.978
It is impossible.

44
00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:13.212
Your turn. Say: Impossible.

45
00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.312
Impossible.

46
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.472
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:25.570
Visal, write two sentences about something you wish were different.

48
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:36.827
I wish I had more free time. I wish I lived near the sea. After wish we use the past simple for a present situation that we want to change.

49
00:02:37.917 --> 00:02:39.324
What about the past?

50
00:02:40.417 --> 00:02:51.486
For a past regret, we use the past perfect: I wish I had studied more. If only is stronger and more emotional: If only I had listened to my mother!

51
00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:53.770
How does would work?

52
00:02:54.883 --> 00:03:10.289
I wish you would stop talking so loudly. Wish + would complains about someone's behaviour or asks for change. We do not use it with I: not I wish I would. After wish, use were for all persons.

53
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:13.177
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.017 --> 00:03:19.081
Grammar focus: Wish and if only: past simple, past perfect, would.

55
00:03:19.381 --> 00:03:20.568
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:21.283 --> 00:03:23.027
I wish I had more free time.

57
00:03:23.917 --> 00:03:25.812
I wish I had studied more.

58
00:03:26.717 --> 00:03:28.565
I wish you would stop talking.

59
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:39.600
Wish + past simple = present wish. Wish + past perfect = past regret. Wish + would = complaint or request. Use were for all persons.

60
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:43.803
Be careful! Don't say: I wish I will be rich.

61
00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.836
Say: I wish I were rich.

62
00:03:48.136 --> 00:03:49.926
Use the past after wish.

63
00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:53.316
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.089
If Only….

65
00:03:55.389 --> 00:03:57.192
I wish I had more free time.

66
00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.885
I wish I lived near the sea, but it is far away.

67
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.143
I wish I had studied harder last year.

68
00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.645
If only I could fly!

69
00:04:07.633 --> 00:04:10.144
It is impossible, but wishing is fun.

70
00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:15.003
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.328
I wish I blank a car. (present)

72
00:04:18.628 --> 00:04:21.562
A, have. B, had. C, would have.

73
00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.740
The answer is B: had.

74
00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:30.861
I wish I blank harder last year. (past)

75
00:04:31.161 --> 00:04:34.710
A, studied. B, had studied. C, would study.

76
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.278
The answer is B: had studied.

77
00:04:41.417 --> 00:04:43.300
I wish you blank stop shouting.

78
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.429
A, would. B, had. C, were.

79
00:04:49.967 --> 00:04:51.571
The answer is A: would.

80
00:04:52.717 --> 00:04:53.880
Which is correct?

81
00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:59.540
A, I wish I was rich.. B, I wish I were rich.. C, I wish I will be rich..

82
00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.866
The answer is B: I wish I were rich..

83
00:05:07.017 --> 00:05:09.527
According to the reading, where does the writer live?

84
00:05:09.827 --> 00:05:13.991
A, far from the sea. B, near the sea. C, in a village.

85
00:05:17.533 --> 00:05:19.695
The answer is A: far from the sea.

86
00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.226
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:25.083 --> 00:05:27.919
Write two sentences about something you wish were different.

88
00:05:36.717 --> 00:05:38.136
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:38.436 --> 00:05:47.813
I wish I had more time to read. I wish I had started learning English earlier. The first wish is about the present, and the second is about the past.

90
00:05:48.113 --> 00:05:49.741
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:57.377
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and wish and if only: past simple, past perfect, would.

92
00:05:57.677 --> 00:06:01.479
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

93
00:06:01.779 --> 00:06:04.640
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:08.069
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

